{"availability":"available","full":"OHDSI/CommonDataModel","name":"CommonDataModel","description":"Definition and DDLs for the OMOP Common Data Model (CDM)","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":1089,"forks":512,"created":"2014-10-14T20:20:22Z","updated":"2026-10-09T16:42:21Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ohdsi.github.io/CommonDataModel","topics":[],"demo":"https://ohdsi.github.io/CommonDataModel","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:30.024Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:30.024Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:30.024Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:30.024Z","stars":1089,"forks":512}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This module will demonstrate two different ways the CDM R package can be used to create the CDM tables in your environment. First, it uses the buildRelease function to create the DDL files on your machine, intended for end users that wish to generate these scripts from R without the need to clone or download the source code from github. The SQL scripts that are created through this process are available as zip files as part of the latest release. They are also available on the master branch here.","Second, the script shows the executeDdl function that will connect up to your SQL client directly (assuming your dbms is one of the supported dialects) and instantiate the tables through R."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OHDSI/CommonDataModel/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7faa145054228d38048c53b42be85d5be4bb466f8759c0896d6b7bf85dc49aef","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:30.129Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:30.129Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This module will demonstrate two different ways the CDM R package can be used to create the CDM tables in your environment. First, it uses the buildRelease function to create the DDL files on your machine, intended for end users that wish to generate these scripts fro